content.text:
Here’s a cleaned-up version of your page that fixes HTML structure, merges duplicate CSS, styles your project/cert blocks, and adds an **“Ask about my background”** panel that POSTs JSON to **`/api/chat`** (matches your assignment: browser never sees the API key—you implement that route on the server).

### What was wrong
- **Duplicate `<nav>` styling** — two competing rule sets (`nav` vs `.navbar`).
- **Invalid nesting** — `<p><p>...</p>` in About.
- **Broken document** — **`</body>` appeared twice**; Matrix `<canvas>`/`</script>` sat outside the proper body structure.
- **Hero overlay** — `.hero` needs **`position: relative`** so `::before` lays over the hero, not misaligned.

### Save this as `index.html` (and keep `images/cyber-bg.jpg` paths the same)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Venkata Naga Kiran Katari | Cybersecurity Portfolio</title>
<style>
html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  background: #0b0f19;
  color: white;
}

/* Navbar */
.navbar {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  background: #020617;
  padding: 15px 0;
  z-index: 1000;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #1e293b;
}

.nav-container {
  width: min(1100px, 85%);
  margin: auto;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
}

.nav-logo a {
  color: #00ff9c;
  font-size: 22px;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.nav-menu {
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 22px;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.nav-menu a {
  text-decoration: none;
  color: white;
  font-size: 16px;
  transition: color 0.3s;
}

.nav-menu a:hover { color: #00ff9c; }

.btn {
  display: inline-block;
  background: #00ff9c;
  color: #020617;
  padding: 14px 30px;
  font-size: 16px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-decoration: none;
  box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.6);
}

.btn:hover { filter: brightness(1.05); }

/* Hero */
.hero {
  position: relative;
  min-height: 100vh;
  background-image: url("images/cyber-bg.jpg");
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 0 24px;
}

.hero::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75);
}

.hero-content {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 2;
  max-width: 900px;
}

.hero h1 {
  margin: 0 0 12px;
  font-size: clamp(34px, 6vw, 60px);
  font-weight: bold;
  letter-spacing: 1px;
  text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.5);
}

.hero p {
  color: #cbd5e1;
  font-size: 18px;
  margin: 0 0 24px;
}

/* Sections */
section {
  padding: 100px 10%;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #1e293b;
}

section:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }

h2 {
  color: #00ff9c;
  margin: 0 0 20px;
}

.skills {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
  gap: 20px;
}

.card, .project-card, .cert-card {
  background: #111827;
  padding: 20px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  border: 1px solid #1e293b;
}

.project-card h3, .cert-card h3 {
  margin-top: 0;
  color: #e2e8f0;
}

.project-card p, .cert-card p {
  color: #cbd5e1;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.project-card + .project-card,
.cert-card + .cert-card {
  margin-top: 20px;
}

/* AI assistant */
.assistant-box {
  background: #111827;
  border: 1px solid #1e293b;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 20px;
  max-width: 720px;
}

.assistant-box label {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
  color: #cbd5e1;
}

.assistant-box textarea {
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 120px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  border-radius: 8px;
  border: 1px solid #334155;
  background: #0b0f19;
  color: #e2e8f0;
  padding: 12px;
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 15px;
  resize: vertical;
}

.assistant-actions {
  display: flex;
  gap: 12px;
  align-items: center;
  margin-top: 12px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.assistant-actions button {
  background: #00ff9c;
  border: none;
  padding: 12px 22px;
  font-size: 15px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-weight: bold;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: #020617;
}

.assistant-actions button:disabled {
  opacity: 0.6;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

.hint {
  color: #94a3b8;
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

.reply {
  margin-top: 16px;
  padding: 14px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  background: #0b0f19;
  border: 1px solid #334155;
  color: #e2e8f0;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
  min-height: 48px;
}

footer {
  text-align: center;
  padding: 40px;
  background: #020617;
}

a.link { color: #00ff9c; }

#matrix {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  z-index: -1;
  pointer-events: none;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<canvas id="matrix" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

<nav class="navbar" aria-label="Primary">
  <div class="nav-container">
    <div class="nav-logo">
      <a href="#">Kiran</a>
    </div>
    <ul class="nav-menu">
      <li><a href="#about">About</a></li>
      <li><a href="#skills">Skills</a></li>
      <li><a href="#projects">Projects</a></li>
      <li><a href="#certifications">Certifications</a></li>
      <li><a href="#assistant">AI Assistant</a></li>
      <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <h1>Venkata Naga Kiran Katari</h1>
    <p>Cybersecurity Graduate Student | Ethical Hacking | Network Security</p>
    <a class="btn" href="CV-KIRAN.pdf" download>Download Resume</a>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="about">
  <h2>About Me</h2>
  <p>
    I am a technically motivated professional with hands-on experience in networking,
    cybersecurity fundamentals, and systems support.
  </p>
  <p>
    I have a strong interest in enterprise networking, infrastructure security, and automation.
    I enjoy understanding how systems work end-to-end and improving them through better design,
    monitoring, and security practices. Alongside my professional experience, I continuously
    build projects and labs to strengthen my real-world skills.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am currently pursuing a Master’s degree in Computer Science at Rowan University while
    complementing my education with industry certifications and practical cybersecurity projects.
  </p>
  <p>📍 Based in Philadelphia, PA</p>
</section>

<section id="skills">
  <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
  <div class="skills">
    <div class="card">Python</div>
    <div class="card">Java</div>
    <div class="card">C</div>
    <div class="card">SQL</div>
    <div class="card">Linux</div>
    <div class="card">Network Security</div>
    <div class="card">Ethical Hacking</div>
    <div class="card">SIEM / SOC</div>
    <div class="card">Burp Suite</div>
    <div class="card">Nmap</div>
    <div class="card">Wireshark</div>
    <div class="card">Splunk</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="projects">
  <h2>Projects</h2>

  <div class="project-card">
    <h3>Enhancing IoT Security Through Anomaly Detection and Intrusion Prevention in Cyber-Physical Systems</h3>
    <p>
      Developed an advanced intrusion detection system to enhance IoT security in cyber-physical environments using
      supervised deep learning models including CNN, LSTM, and DNN architectures. The system was evaluated on
      benchmark datasets such as KDDCup99, NSL-KDD, and UNSW-NB15, achieving accuracies of 100%, 95.1%, and
      87.4% respectively. A Flask-based web application was deployed to demonstrate real-time anomaly detection with
      standardized data preprocessing. This research was published in the Proceedings of ICCIET 2024 by Atlantis Press.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-card">
    <h3>Keylogger – Capturing Keystrokes</h3>
    <p>
      Developed a proof-of-concept keylogger application capable capturing keyboard input events through a graphical
      user interface. This project was created for cybersecurity awareness and educational demonstrations, highlighting
      how keystroke monitoring works and emphasizing the importance of endpoint protection and ethical security practices.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-card">
    <h3>Student Database Management System</h3>
    <p>
      Developed a web-based Student Database Management System (SDMS) using PHP, HTML, CSS, and MySQL to
      manage student records, faculty information, attendance tracking, exam data, and registration details. Implemented
      full CRUD operations across relational tables and incorporated views, stored procedures, functions, and triggers to
      maintain data consistency and integrity.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="certifications">
  <h2>Certifications</h2>

  <div class="cert-card">
    <h3>Microsoft Azure Fundamentals (AZ-900)</h3>
    <p>
      Microsoft certification demonstrating foundational knowledge of cloud concepts,
      Azure services, security, compliance, pricing, and cloud architecture.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="cert-card">
