    For hiring or official inquiries, please use email or LinkedIn in the Contact section.
  </p>

  <div class="assistant-box">
    <label for="usermsg">Your question</label>
    <textarea id="usermsg" placeholder='Example: "What IoT security project did you publish?"'></textarea>

    <div class="assistant-actions">
      <button type="button" id="sendBtn">Ask</button>
      <span class="hint" id="status"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="reply" id="reply" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="contact">
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Email: kirankatari99@gmail.com</p>
  <p>
    GitHub:
    <a class="link" href="https://github.com/kirankatari" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/kirankatari</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    LinkedIn:
    <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/venkata-naga-kiran-katari-b094361a9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">linkedin.com/in/venkata-naga-kiran-katari</a>
  </p>
</section>

<footer>
  © 2026 Venkata Naga Kiran Katari | Cybersecurity Portfolio
</footer>

<script>
/* Matrix background */
const canvas = document.getElementById("matrix");
const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");

function resizeCanvas() {
  canvas.height = window.innerHeight;
  canvas.width = window.innerWidth;
}
resizeCanvas();
window.addEventListener("resize", resizeCanvas);

const letters = "01";
const fontSize = 16;
let columns = Math.floor(canvas.width / fontSize);
let drops = Array.from({ length: columns }, () => 1);

window.addEventListener("resize", () => {
  columns = Math.floor(canvas.width / fontSize);
  drops = Array.from({ length: columns }, () => 1);
});

function draw() {
  ctx.fillStyle = "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)";
  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

  ctx.fillStyle = "#00ff9c";
  ctx.font = fontSize + "px monospace";

  for (let i = 0; i < drops.length; i++) {
    const text = letters.charAt(Math.floor(Math.random() * letters.length));
    ctx.fillText(text, i * fontSize, drops[i] * fontSize);

    if (drops[i] * fontSize > canvas.height && Math.random() > 0.975) drops[i] = 0;
    drops[i]++;
  }
}

setInterval(draw, 33);

/* AI assistant -> server route /api/chat (implement on VPS) */
const sendBtn = document.getElementById("sendBtn");
const usermsg = document.getElementById("usermsg");
const replyEl = document.getElementById("reply");
const statusEl = document.getElementById("status");

sendBtn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
  const message = usermsg.value.trim();
  replyEl.textContent = "";
  statusEl.textContent = "";

  if (!message) {
    replyEl.textContent = "Please type a question.";
    return;
  }

  sendBtn.disabled = true;
  statusEl.textContent = "Thinking…";

  try {
    const response = await fetch("/api/chat", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({ message })
    });

    let data = null;
    try { data = await response.json(); } catch (_) { /* non-JSON */ }

    if (!response.ok || !data || typeof data.reply !== "string") {
      throw new Error((data && data.error) ? data.error : "bad_response");
    }

    replyEl.textContent = data.reply;
    statusEl.textContent = "";
  } catch (_) {
    statusEl.textContent = "";
    replyEl.textContent =
      "Sorry — I can’t reach the assistant right now. Please try again in a minute, or contact me directly at kirankatari99@gmail.com.";
  } finally {
    sendBtn.disabled = false;
  }
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What you must add on the server (for full credit)

1. **`POST /api/chat`** accepts JSON `{ "message": "..." }`, reads your API key **only server-side**, calls OpenAI/Gemini/Claude/etc., returns JSON like `{ "reply": "..." }`.
2. **Nginx** proxies `location /api/` to your internal app (e.g. PHP-FPM script, Flask on `127.0.0.1:5001`, Node on a Unix socket)—so nothing hits the AI provider directly from the browser.
3. **System prompt** on the server includes the same facts as your site (Rowan MS CS, Philadelphia, projects, certs, skills) and instructs the model not to invent details.

If you tell me your stack (**PHP, Python, or Node**) and provider (**OpenAI vs Gemini**), I can give you a drop-in server file and a matching `location` block for Nginx.

